scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: mash
run_id: 4
total_caught: 2
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 13
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 35.1
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA's security.rs includes a test for 'silent error swallowing' which
    targets exactly this pattern of from_file_or_default masking parse/permission
    errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Reviewer verified CWE-209 but only checked for token/password/secret/Bearer/api_key\
    \ leaks in Display/Debug. The actual issue \u2014 Io(#[error(transparent)]) forwarding\
    \ full OS error paths to stderr \u2014 was not flagged. The security tests check\
    \ a narrower scope than the real vulnerability."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented sanitize_header_value at client.rs:19-21 stripping \\\
    r and \\n from tenant ID values, and TEA wrote CRLF injection tests in security.rs:57-85.\
    \ However, the deeper issue of using raw String instead of axiathon-core's validated\
    \ TenantId was not addressed \u2014 only the symptom was mitigated."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged toml version mismatch with spec (finding #6) but did
    not flag the 6 dependencies using direct version strings instead of workspace
    = true. The Cargo.toml diff shows only 2 lines changed.'
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #10 explicitly marks ''tokens in the TOML file are silently
    ignored'' as VERIFIED (correct behavior). The pipeline treats the silent ignoring
    as a security feature rather than recognizing it as a usability/security gap where
    users believe they''re authenticated when they''re not.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged a different vacuous test (piped_output_defaults_to_json,
    finding #5) but did not identify the config test with assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) where the OR makes the assertion always true.'
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test using 'let _ = config' with no
    assert_eq! checks on server() or token() for the default config.
